1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,160
They fired a laser

2
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,520
into a thunderstorm—

3
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:04,310
and the lightning followed it.

4
00:00:04,310 --> 00:00:06,310
You see, air normally resists

5
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:07,810
the flow of electricity.

6
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:08,950
But this machine fired

7
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:10,390
a thousand laser pulses

8
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:11,420
every second,

9
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,330
stripping electrons

10
00:00:12,330 --> 00:00:13,330
from air molecules

11
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,640
and heating a narrow channel

12
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,830
through the sky.

13
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:16,920
That gave electricity

14
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,790
an easier path to travel.

15
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,310
So when lightning erupted upward

16
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:21,630
from a nearby tower,

17
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:22,270
part of the bolt

18
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:23,200
followed that channel

19
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,610
for over 160 feet.

20
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:26,600
A normal lightning rod

21
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,620
only reaches as high

22
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:28,940
as its metal tip.

23
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,740
But these scientists extended one

24
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:31,880
into the sky—

25
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:33,400
using the air itself.

